A solid circular bar of length $L = 1.2$ m tapers linearly from diameter $d_1 = 30$ mm (large end) to $d_2 = 20$ mm (small end). The bar is loaded in tension with an axial load $P = 40$ kN. The material has yield strength 250 MPa and Young's modulus $E = 200$ GPa. Determine:

i. the axial (working) stress at the large and small ends;
ii. the factor of safety against yielding based on the maximum stress;
iii. the total change in length (elongation) of the tapered bar under the load.
